<title>CANADA: Hammond Mfg plans share buyback.</title>
<headline>Hammond Mfg plans share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>GUELPH, Ontario 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hammond Manufacturing Co Ltd said it intends to buy up to 400,000 shares or about five percent of its more than 8.8 million Class A subordinate voting shares.</p>
<p>&quot;The corporation believes that the current level the shares are trading on the Toronto Stock Exchange is below their fair value,&quot; the electronics and electrical parts maker said. Shares closed at 1.57 on March 21.</p>
<p>The buy-back is scheduled to start March 26 and will continue to until March 25, 1998. The firm said in 1996 it bought and cancelled 239,700 Class A shares.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109))</p>
</text>
